You miss hcobb's point. All characters start out basic in the weapon
they start out with, but they can all get to at least expert in it. The
same thing is true for both quest artifacts and guaranteed first gifts:
if those are weapons, the relevant class can get to expert with them.
But those are not the cases he was talking about.

The point is that when you get crowned, you may also get a weapon.
_That_ weapon is always a long sword or broadsword, depending only on
alignment and not on class. This means that several classes can, on
crowning, receive a gift they can't get any further than basic in. In
fact, most will receive a gift in which they start out restricted, and
are only able to reach basic in _after_ crowning.
Tourists are hardly unique in this, so I don't see why hcobb is
complaining about them. Sure, you could give them a class-specific gift,
but why stop there? Why not give Arcs, who start out even less capable
with long swords than Tou's, Grayswandir instead of Vorpy or Excalibur?
Why not gift Pri's with Mjollnir? Mons and Wizs get a spellbook, not
because they're bad with swords, but because they shouldn't be weapons
users at all. The rest should just be grateful to be given (and usually
unrestricted in, as well!) what is, after all, a pretty decent weapon.

> Tourists get loads of starting money. 

For values of "loads" that can be as low as 1. Not getting enough to
make even a single protection sacrifice is quite possible, which makes
the protection racket a strategy which not all Tourists can follow.

